      "index": 1,
      "text": "Purpose The purpose of this activity is for you to practice applying what you are learning. This activity does count for points toward your grade, you will need to show your work, and you are graded on correctness. However, you have multiple attempts to improve your score. Instructions You will see one question at a time. A good method for working on this assignment is to watch the posted lecture and stop it when people in the Zoom lecture are working out a problem, and work it for yourself. Then continue the lecture video to see the solution worked out. The question in the asynchronous assignment may be exactly the same, or it may have different values, or it may require a slightly different solution. Show your work on paper, as you will be required to upload your work at the end of the assignment. If you do not show reasonable work for this, you will not get credit for the activity. There is a short 50 word essay question at the end of the assignment asking you to discuss the concepts of the day's material. You are required to complete this question to get credit for the day's assignment. To get a high-quality scan for uploading to this quiz tool, use a scanning app to scan your handwritten work, and upload your scanned document. Here are some resources to help you get started: Get a clear scan that is automatically cropped and formatted into multi-page PDF files by installing a scanning app on your phone. Here are some recommended free apps: Genius Scan (Links to an external site.) (available for iPhone, iPad, and Android devices). Find it at the Apple Store (Links to an external site.) or Google Play. (Links to an external site.) Microsoft Office Lens (Links to an external site.) (available for iPhone, iPad and Android). Find the app at the Apple Store or Google Play. CamScanner (Links to an external site.) (available for iPhone and Android). This app has the most features, and the basic package is free. However, there are subscription options available if you want to pay for the more advanced features. Find this app at the Apple Store or Google Play. Scanner Pro (Links to an external site.) (available for iPhone and iPad only). If you do not have a smartphone for scanning your work, please scan your work from a home scanner, take screenshots of your work and submit those, or type out and attach a file of a written description of the steps you took. If you need assistance, please reach out for help from the Wormhole, office hours or email."
