      "text": "Move To... This element is a more accessible alternative to drag & drop reordering. Press Enter or Space to move this question. Question 1 1 / 1 pts Edit this Question Delete this Question 0 numerical_question 111085047 <p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">The angular velocity of a spinning disk is given by ω(t) = A - B t<sup>2</sup>. <span>Starting from t</span><sub>0</sub><span>&nbsp;= 0.0s, at what time does the disk reverse direction?</span> Consider the case where A = 18 rad/s and B = 0.50 rad/s<sup>3</sup>.</span></p> <p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">Enter your answer in seconds. (Just enter the number, not the units.)</span></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> The angular velocity of a spinning disk is given by ω(t) = A - B t2. Starting from t0 = 0.0s, at what time does the disk reverse direction? Consider the case where A = 18 rad/s and B = 0.50 rad/s3. Enter your answer in seconds. (Just enter the number, not the units.)"
