      "text": "Move To... This element is a more accessible alternative to drag & drop reordering. Press Enter or Space to move this question. Question 2 1 / 1 pts Edit this Question Delete this Question 0 numerical_question 111091671 <p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">The angular velocity of a spinning disk is given by ω(t) = A - B t<sup>2</sup>.&nbsp;Through what angle does the disk turn between t<sub>0</sub>&nbsp;= 0.0s and the time at which it reverses its direction of rotation?</span></p> <p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Consider the case where A = 18 rad/s and B = 0.50 rad/s<sup>3</sup>.</span></p> <p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Enter your answer in radians.</span></p> The angular velocity of a spinning disk is given by ω(t) = A - B t2. Through what angle does the disk turn between t0 = 0.0s and the time at which it reverses its direction of rotation? Consider the case where A = 18 rad/s and B = 0.50 rad/s3. Enter your answer in radians."
