      "index": 21,
      "text": "Move To... This element is a more accessible alternative to drag & drop reordering. Press Enter or Space to move this question. Question 3 0 / 1 pts Edit this Question Delete this Question 0 essay_question 111091669 <p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Using your own words, enter at least 50 words describing the concepts underlying the topic for today. You need to completely answer this question to get credit for this assignment.</span></p> Using your own words, enter at least 50 words describing the concepts underlying the topic for today. You need to completely answer this question to get credit for this assignment. Your Answer: Today’s topic was about rotational motion and how it relates to regular straight-line motion. Instead of position, velocity, and acceleration, rotational motion uses angle, angular velocity, and angular acceleration. Angular velocity describes how fast an object rotates, while angular acceleration describes how fast that angular velocity changes. We also learned that when angular velocity changes with time, we may need calculus, such as derivatives and integrals, to find quantities like angular displacement."
